<title>USA: Spatializer found not infringing patent.</title>
<headline>Spatializer found not infringing patent.</headline>
<dateline>WOODLAND HILLS, Calif. 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spatializer Audio Laboratories Inc said Friday that U.S. District Court Judge William D. Keller ruled in the company's favor, granting its motion for summary judgment of non-infringment in a lawsuit filed by QSound Labs Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;This ruling finds that the Spatializer integrated circuit does not infringe QSound patents,&quot; Spatializer said.</p>
<p>The company said it intends to pursue its claim for damages resulting from QSound's interference with Spatializer's business, and file a motion for summary judgment seeking to invalidate the QSound patents.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
